hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:3c01cad7a24e0deb09a1aee718c4ffa3018e80e040529ac81d5f997745cc8759","file":"preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-spherical-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex","line":669,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"0ab1ecd4c71a404cbd74d2536d14c1c7a65b02b50fe35856de5cbaba6d97dc28","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-spherical-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:3c01cad7a24e0deb09a1aee718c4ffa3018e80e040529ac81d5f997745cc8759","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-spherical-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex#L669"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:spherical}\nFor fixed interval weights, uniformly on compact sets of nonnegative\nnondecreasing step field values,\n\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:spherical-dual}\nl_n(h)\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\min_{q_0\\le\\cdots\\le q_{k-1}\\,;\\ 0\\le q_i<1}\n       \\left\\{S(q)-\\sum_i w_i h_i q_i\\right\\}\n\\end{equation}\n\nas $n\\to\\infty$. Furthermore, for each fixed $0\\le B<1$, if $0\\le q(u)\\le B$ a.e. is nondecreasing and\n\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:stationary-field}\n2h(u)=A_q(q(u)),\\qquad A_q(r):=\\int_0^r\\frac{dt}{D_q(t)^2}\\quad(0\\le r<1),\n\\end{equation}\n\nthen\n\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:spherical-uniform}\nl_n(h)=S(q)-\\int_0^1 hq+o(1),\n\\end{equation}\n\nwhere the error tends to zero uniformly over these $q$."}
